If you have multiple volumes in your file domain, ie when you do a showfdmn
you see more than one volume listed.  You can reduce that file domain by
rmvol (AdvFS Utilities required) command.  You CAN NOT shrink an AdvFS
domain using LSM shrinkby or shrinkto commands (also UFS can't be done).

Your only choice may be to vdump/vrestore and reallocate the file domain.
If you do this break the file domain into 4-6 volumes (Digital's ROT) so you
will have the flexibility to reduce and/or add at users whims (this will
require AdvFS Utilities).

Bruce

