Digital UNIX V4.0 has several provisions for automating an installation.

The install.cdf file (also known as "clone install") is a supported method for
configuring
Digital UNIX (dunix) systems without operator intervention.  It is available
starting
with dunix V4.0B, and is documented in the Installation Guide, Appendix C.

Also, there are hooks, also documented in Appendix C I believe, to allow
arbitrary user-defined
actions at crititcal points in the installation process.

For one-time events that must occur on reboot, see the the it(8) and itruns(8)
manpages.

