I promise you you'll be happier in the long run if you get perl (there is a
setld perl kit on
ftp.digital.com:/pub/DEC/) and then get the ftp extension for perl and use
that.  It allows you
to completely automate ftp transactions *reliably*.

Another solution is to get TCL/TK, and then build the expect extension, which
allows the automating
of arbitrary command-line dialogs.

