We implemented what you are describing using Digital Unix 4.0, ASE
cluster, Alpha 1000 5/500, 128 MB, 2 shared SCSI buses, Mirroring,
Advanced Files System, LSM,  X.25, X.400, X.500 and finally the
application, DEC/EDI. The only thing we left out was SNA.

Think about your requirements very carefully, I was fortunate to have
the assistance of an experienced Trucluster sysadmin from DEC (paid
for by the project) which made things go very well

I would have preferred an X.25 gateway on the network, however, I was
forced into bring direct X.25 connections to the 2 systems which
complicates things for failover. Accomodating X.25 for failover is
probably the most complex piece of planning you will have to consider.
We have an X.25 hunt group to the two systems which therefore bothe
respond to the X.25 packets. you must then configure X.25
appropriately. In our case the X.25 packets are delivered to the X.400
Mailbus package and the Mailbus package has to know which node to
forward the X.400 messages to.

Hope this helps.
Regards
	Andrew Stafford
	VMS Systems Support
	ISM / IBM Global Services
