Hello,

We have an additional Fast/Wide SCSI Adapter (IntraServer ITI-6100) in a DEC
AlphaStation 200 4/166 running Digital Unix 4.0B. The Console SRM firmware
version is 6.8-2.

From the >>> prompt, all devices attached to this adapter can been see by
the "show dev" at the correct SCSI ID. Some of the devices use a SCSI ID
higher than 7 there is still no problems.

However, when we boot the system, it does not detect the devices above 7.
The same device, when reconfigured to SCSI ID 5 is seen by the operating
system. The O/S can see the controller and loads the driver for it but just
does NOT display the devices above SCSI ID 7.

I have heard that VMS has a similar problem. Has anybody seen this problem
and if so, it there a way around it ?

Any comments would be greatly appreciated.

