I made a shell script based on the following principle :
On local host : my tape : /dev/rmt0h

<root@remote> cat > /.rhosts
root local
^D
<root@local> cat > /.rhosts
root remote
^D

For backuping :

<root@local> rsh remote -l root dump 0uf - /usr | dd of=3D/def/rmt0h
obs=3D20b
or
<root@local> rsh remote -l root tar cBf - /usr | dd of=3D/def/rmt0h
obs=3D20b

For restoring
if dump :
<root@remote> rsh local -l root dd if=3D/dev/rmt0h ibf=3D20b | restore xf=
 -
or
<root@local> dd if=3D/dev/rmt0h ibs=3D20b | rsh remote -l root restore xf=
 -

if tar :
<root@remote> rsh local -l root dd if=3D/dev/rmt0h ibf=3D20b | tar xvf -
or
<root@local> dd if=3D/dev/rmt0h ibs=3D20b | rsh remote -l root tar xvf -

hope it helps you !

