On Mon, 21 Sep 1998 17:05:33 +0200, Hans Westerback
<edthwes@unixcenter.ericsson.se> wrote:

>Hi
>
>we're running DUNIX 4.0D, and at Eureka I recently heard about DoP,
>which should be able to let some users use root privs for specified
>commands. I have found /usr/sbin/dop, but how should it be used? The
>slides I saw indicated there should be a dopconfig, but I can't find it.
>
>Any hints?

/etc/doprc

Example:
----------
adduser{
  {users { tim michael }}
  {path { /usr/sbin/adduser }}
}

removeuser {
  {groups { admin }}
  {path { /usr/sbin/removeuser }}
}
----------
Users tim and michael can now use "/usr/sbin/dop adduser".

You can add new commands with "dop -a full_path_of_command", and
delete one with "dop -d name_of_command".


