I need help using vrestore to restore files from a vdump operation that
spanned multiple tapes.

I have some large ADVFS filesets (on an LSM volume) that I backup to 8mm
tape using vdump. The filesets are large enough to span several 8mm tapes.
This seems to be supported: vdump prompts for me to load tape 2, tape 3, etc.
as it proceeds.

Today I tried to retrieve a file from this set of tapes. I loaded the first
tape, and gave the command "vrestore -i -f /dev/nrmt0h". I selected the files
I wanted restored, and gave the "extract" command. Vrestore read through
the first tape, and then prompted me:

vrestore: Change Tapes: Mount tape# 0002
vrestore: Press RETURN when tape is mounted...

I did this, and got the error messages

vrestore: can't open device file </dev/nrmt0h>; [13] Permission denied
vrestore: do you want to retry? y
vrestore: Press RETURN when tape is mounted...
vrestore: can't open device file </dev/nrmt0h>; [13] Permission denied
vrestore: do you want to retry?

etc. This happens consistently on any multi-tape archive written with vdump.
Does anyone know how to get vrestore to handle multiple tapes? I tried the
obvious thing of starting vrestore with the second tape, and it gagged.

BTW, I'm using DU 4.0C (Rev. 564.32) with whatever aggregate patch kit was
current on May 6, if that matters.

Thanks for any help...
