>vrestore: can't open device file </dev/nrmt0h>; [13] Permission denied
>vrestore: do you want to retry? y
>vrestore: Press RETURN when tape is mounted...
>vrestore: can't open device file </dev/nrmt0h>; [13] Permission denied
>vrestore: do you want to retry?
>
>etc. This happens consistently on any multi-tape archive written with vdump.
>Does anyone know how to get vrestore to handle multiple tapes? I tried the
>obvious thing of starting vrestore with the second tape, and it gagged.

This one I recognize from experiencing the same restoring from DAT
cartridges.  I expect like any experienced user of tapes that you
have engaged the write lock on the tape so it will not get written
over accidentally if left in the drive.  Well, there is a bug(feature?)
in either the vrestore code or the tape interface code that causes
the open of the second and succeeding tapes to fail if the write lock
is on.  Load the continuation tapes without write protection and the
open will work.  This problem was there in 4.0b, and is still there on
the 4.0d systems here.  I reported it to the sysadmin here some time
back, I have not heard that there was a fix for this yet.  If anyone
knows of a pertinent patch or update, I would like to know of it.

