wuyi@cyberway.com.sg wrote:
> 
> On my Alpha server ,which OS version is V4.0D , I always found the
> error : task table is full .  When the problem happened , the system
> almost hang and I had to reboot the system . Anyone can tell me
> what does it mean and how to increase task finger . Thanks

This means just what it says, no more entries in task table.

The size of the task table is statical and built into the kernel. It can either
be changed explicitly or implicitly. The static configuration file for the
kernel is /sys/conf/<YOUR_SYSTEM_NAME_IN_CAPS>

IF specified maxproc like

maxproc	1024

THEN

Task Table Size = maxproc

ELSE

Task Table Size = maxusers * 4 + 1 (or something like that)

ENDIF

In other words, if you set maxproc, that's it. If you don't then the system will
calculate some appropriate default value.

Nix.





