Paul Chapin wrote:
> 
> Any ideas why dtadvfs has suddenly started to fail telling me that it
> "Failed to make agent connection to host".    I've done a fair amount of
> system upgrades this summer, but nothing that should have caused any dtadvfs
> problem.

The GUI part "dtadvfs" is only a client, which connects to any host on the
network running (of course 4.0D) advfsd (AdvFS Daemon). Whether you'll be
allowed to access AdvFS on that host, depends on
/var/opt/advfsd/socket/hosts.allow file.

I have expirienced problems when I setup DNS. Make sure that:

1. you have "querry /etc/hosts first" in /etc/svc.conf
2. you have your host's name in /etc/hosts

Nix.




