>dump file?  On VMS I would have performed a restore to the NUL device
>and then checked for any errors, but I can't see how to do that with DEC
>unix's restore.

You can read back the archive using dd(1).  Left to itself dump would
have used a 10 KB block size:

dd if=/dev/rmt#h of=/dev/null bs=10k

If you want to spot check for undetected data errors, restore some
files at random to a different file system and if they apparently
haven't changed with respect to the original compare them.

>Bob

