> Another related poser: are there any specific requirements in terms of
> memory slot usage with the 3000/400? Like, right now 8 of the 16 slots are
> occupied with 8 MB SIMMs. Can I just replace these with larger and faster
> SIMMs, or can I only add 8 more 8 MB SIMMs? The owners guide does not say
> what the deal is.

    You can add denser SIMMs, and the only restriction is that the higher
density SIMM sets have to go in the lowest numbered banks.... so of
course, you have to pull all those 8 Mbyte SIMMs and reolcate them in
higher-numbered banks (unless you got lucky and found enough higher
density SIMMs to fill all the banks). Still, Digital _did_ put those handy
pull tabs in there for a reason.

    Another useful thing to do while you're in there (if it hasn't been
done already) is to move the &^%*ing EEPROM upgrade jumper to the "allow"
(or whatever it's called) pins, so you don't have to yank apart the box
every time you do a firmware upgrade.

