Depends on how heavily the network is loaded.  A lightly loaded network
probably won't notice a little rwhod.  A significantly loaded network
can slip into a broadcast storm, so it's best to keep unecessary
broadcast turned off.  Most of the nets I work with have a policy
requiring rwhod and friends to be turned off.

