Stephen Cook wrote:
> 
> Hi everyone,
> 
> I have a Digital 4100 running Digital Unix V3.2G with LSM and AdvFs
> enabled.  I want to update it to the latest and greatest V4.0D,
> however I do not have enough disk space on the root file system.
> 
> In my Digital course several years ago the instructor told me to
> ensure that I never ran out of space on the root file system as I did
> not want to have to expande it.  This implies that it is possible.

Highly unlikely. Both UFS and AdvFS (or any other FS) set some of it's
parameters acording to the partition size. If you just change the partition
size, the FS will stay the same. Any tool trying to change that would need to
rebuild superblock, i-node tables and almost everything else.

This, effectively, equals to backing data up somewhere, creating new FS and
restoring data from the backup, this way or the other. And that is exactly what
you can do, "vdump .... disklabel ... (LSM tools) ... mkfdmn ... mkfset ...
vrestore"

Nix.




