   the disk using disklabel, making sure to *only* expand the root 
   partition (typically "a") into the swap partition (typically "b")
   thus you don't have to worry about having to dump and save the whole
   disk.  You dump the root, repartition root-swap, make a new file system
   using newfs, and restore from you initial dump. 

2) if your machine has two disks, you can boot from the second while
   expanding the first and vice-versa.


