Stephen Cook wrote:
> 
> Hi everyone,
> 
> I have a Digital 4100 running Digital Unix V3.2G with LSM and AdvFs
> enabled.  I want to update it to the latest and greatest V4.0D,
> however I do not have enough disk space on the root file system.
> 
> In my Digital course several years ago the instructor told me to
> ensure that I never ran out of space on the root file system as I did
> not want to have to expande it.  This implies that it is possible.
> 
> So my question is how do I expand the root file system?


Basically I believe the boot loader can't deal with parts on vmunix 
beging mapped of the boot device so rather than make any of the boot
code more insane they have inforced a no expand option for the root
file system domain. If you build the root_domain by hand you must
remember to also inforce this :-

-r  Specifies the file domain as the root domain. This prevents multiple
    volumes in the root domain.  AdvFS supports only one volume in the
    root domain.

If you don't you could simple addvol to root_domain which would probably
keep working for a while till you reboot. Not sure if the mount of
root_domain will fail or it may keep working till vmunix or other
important boot file gets mapped off the primary boot device? In either 
case its not what you want.

	Cheers
		Mark :)



