if you have a second disk, it's easy. partition the second using the same 
layout as the boot disk, but make partition 'a' as big as you want.
Then do disklabel and all this stuff.
Shutdown to single-user mode, 'dd' partition 'a' ffrom systemdisk to partition 
'a' of spare disk. for all other fielssystems you can use 'dump'.

shutdown the machine, change SCSI-id's and boot the new(identical) system.
I do not recommend booting direct from the spare-disk without changing the 
SCSI-id's as in some file a e.g. '/dev/rz0...' will cause problems...

I've done this often under Ultrix, never tested it on OSF1, but there's 
same old partition stuff ...

regards




