> Sung Moon Kang BK94 AA96     | UCLA Mech and Aero Engineering
> sung.kang.bk.94@aya.yale.edu | http://home.att.net/~sungmoonkang/

cleanest way :

Just go to /sys/conf/

# cp BADNAME GOODNAME
edit GODDNAME and change 1st line (ident) to good.

# doconfig -c GOODNAME
# mv /sys/GOODNAME/vmunix /

add goodname in /etc/hosts with your ip Address
then edit /etc/rc.config and change hostname

Tha's all you'll have to do


