These you got in a nice Digital UNIX box, right?

Well, there are two other "boxes", which look more like thick A4 folders. One
holds "On-Line Documentation" and the other holds "Software Layered Products
Library" CDs. There should be 3 of them (only 4.0A had 4 CDs). The first one has
cxx600 with C++ compiler.

Of course, you'll need a special license to run the compiler, "CXX-OSF-USER".

Nix.




